{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Pure.</b> You are pure of eyes so that You do not look upon evil, and the bet is defective, and it is like: ואל אראה ברעתי (and let me not look upon my evil)." "<b>והביט.</b> A verb." "<b>Upon wrongdoing You cannot.</b> According to the way of Your wisdom and Your faithfulness, for You cannot bear, by reason of Your great holiness and Your piety, a thing that is the opposite before You. And this is what he said: תביט — afterward he said: והביט אל עמל לא תוכל — according to the thinking of human beings, who wonder how You keep silent about this, for it is not in the way of truth for the wicked to swallow one more righteous than he; and if he is not perfectly righteous, therefore he wrote: על משמרתי אעמודה ואצפה לנקמתך ולישועתך אקוה."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:59.514957301Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}